# TenkaCloud cloud hosting: development
# Copy to .env in this directory only when that file does not already exist:
#   test -e infrastructure/environments/development/.env || cp infrastructure/environments/development/.env.example infrastructure/environments/development/.env
# Or run make env-init ENV=development to create the missing file interactively.
# Turso setup: make turso-live ENV=development; rotation: make turso-token-rotate ENV=development.
# Edit the empty values, then use make deploy ENV=development.
# このディレクトリの .env にコピーし、空欄を編集してください。既存 .env は上書きしません。

# Must match the directory and selected make ENV value.
# Do not copy another environment's populated .env without changing this value.
ENV=development

# Required for ordinary deployment: organizer's real Cognito invitation address.
# Example only: organizer@example.test (replace; do not deploy with a placeholder).
TENKACLOUD_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# Required for offline --show-setup; also checks the target of actual AWS credentials.
# Use the intended 12-digit hosting account ID. Example only: 123456789012.
ACCOUNT_ID=

# Select the intended AWS region. REGION (if exported) takes precedence.
AWS_REGION=ap-northeast-1

# Cloud control data: dynamodb (default) or turso. Local hosting still uses SQLite.
CDK_PARAM_CONTROL_DATA_BACKEND=dynamodb
# For turso, set both values. Use an existing database and SSM SecureString token
# encrypted with the AWS managed SSM key in the selected account/region.
# Only the parameter name goes into Lambda environment; never put a token here.
# libsql:// and https:// database URLs are accepted. No DynamoDB tables are created.
CDK_PARAM_TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
CDK_PARAM_TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN_PARAMETER_NAME=
# Example parameter name: /TenkaCloud/development/turso/auth-token
# Existing installations cannot switch providers or database URLs automatically.
# make destroy keeps external Turso rows; make destroy-all explicitly resets them.

# Owned tables are deleted by make destroy by default, matching the original behavior.
# Only the exact value true retains DynamoDB tables. This applies at deployment time.
# Re-deploy existing retained/protected stacks with this setting before destroying them.
CDK_PARAM_RETAIN_DATA_TABLES=false

# Use an existing AWS CLI profile or role; never place access keys or tokens here.
# AWS_PROFILE=your-tenkacloud-profile

# make deploy ENV=development reuses the account/region's standard CDKToolkit.
# Only if missing, it runs the pinned official cdk bootstrap, then deploys.
# Ordinary deploy uses --require-approval never, including CI; no extra flag/prompt.
# It displays the target, permission scope and possible AWS charges before creation.
# Standard CDK defaults to AdministratorAccess on its CloudFormation execution role.
# Review that authority and use a caller authorized to bootstrap and deploy.
# The CLI never grants permissions to your profile/role.
# Optional offline preview: make -s deploy ENV=development CLOUD_ARGS="--show-setup"
# Optional bootstrap-only (asks for consent): make deploy ENV=development CLOUD_ARGS="--setup"
# Setup-only automation can use --setup --yes; ordinary deploy needs neither.
# --yes and --setup-if-needed remain optional deployment compatibility flags.
# An existing toolkit is never rewritten; custom execution-policy assertions from
# earlier revisions are unsupported. See infrastructure/BOOTSTRAP-IAM.md.
# destroy keeps its confirmation and empties only exact CFN-owned Delete buckets.
# Retained contents require destroy-all; Retain bucket containers remain.
# The CLI caller needs exact-bucket S3 tagging/version-list/object-delete access,
# separately from CloudFormation execution permissions; see BOOTSTRAP-IAM.md.

# Exported process variables override these values, including an explicit empty value.
# ENV and CDK_PARAM_ENVIRONMENT must agree with this directory.
# Values are single-line KEY=value (optional export, quotes and comments).
# Shell commands, variable expansion and multiline values are not interpreted.

